WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.874 --> 00:00:02.917
Line 3 runs in hall B.

2
00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:08.346
Now a new MES is coming, the system that runs the orders on the floor.

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.879
You lead that IT project for the plant manager.

4
00:00:12.581 --> 00:00:16.517
The IT team builds the MES out and keeps it running.

5
00:00:17.527 --> 00:00:21.103
We follow the project from the first requirement to real use,

6
00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:23.111
through the four topics of the module.

7
00:00:23.796 --> 00:00:26.350
The details come later, in the lessons.

8
00:00:27.677 --> 00:00:30.150
The first topic is Requirements and scope.

9
00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:33.222
What must the MES actually do?

10
00:00:34.227 --> 00:00:39.161
A requirement is something the MES must do, written so that you can check it.

11
00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:44.580
You write them with people who know the work, like the team lead of line 3.

12
00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:48.107
Not everything fits in the first version.

13
00:00:48.811 --> 00:00:51.493
What must be in at go-live, and what can wait?

14
00:00:52.507 --> 00:00:57.162
For requirements we use MoSCoW and a to-be process, the work as it will run.

15
00:00:58.451 --> 00:01:02.144
The second topic is Choosing a vendor, SaaS and contracts.

16
00:01:02.856 --> 00:01:04.644
Where does the MES come from?

17
00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.337
You rarely build an MES yourself.

18
00:01:09.026 --> 00:01:10.779
You buy a package or rent it.

19
00:01:11.557 --> 00:01:14.610
Renting is called SaaS, the vendor runs it for you.

20
00:01:15.615 --> 00:01:17.647
The software vendor makes the package.

21
00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.098
The implementation partner sets it up for you.

22
00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:25.259
Put in one table who does what, our IT team too.

23
00:01:25.976 --> 00:01:28.611
Otherwise one points at the other later.

24
00:01:29.616 --> 00:01:34.956
For choosing we use an RFP, the request for a proposal, and a scoring matrix.

25
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:41.718
The third topic is ERP and MES implementation, from migration to hypercare.

26
00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:44.718
How does the MES really go live?

27
00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:49.925
Go-live is the day the new MES becomes the official system.

28
00:01:50.645 --> 00:01:53.106
The old system then does no new work.

29
00:01:54.186 --> 00:01:56.647
A big bang switches everything at once.

30
00:01:57.329 --> 00:02:00.534
Phased goes line by line, with less risk per step.

31
00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.596
For roll-out we use a pilot and a mock migration.

32
00:02:05.902 --> 00:02:08.247
The fourth topic is Testing and adoption.

33
00:02:08.975 --> 00:02:12.423
Before go-live, does the MES really fit the work?

34
00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:19.237
In the UAT, the user acceptance test, future users check that the MES fits.

35
00:02:20.227 --> 00:02:25.742
Key users, like the team lead of line 3, test with situations from the real work.

36
00:02:26.776 --> 00:02:29.795
After the test the process owners sign the sign-off.

37
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.661
Then the MES is accepted.

38
00:02:33.716 --> 00:02:34.842
And after go-live?

39
00:02:35.573 --> 00:02:38.255
Without use the MES delivers nothing.

40
00:02:39.299 --> 00:02:43.537
For testing we use a test script and triage, sorting the defects.

41
00:02:44.842 --> 00:02:45.957
It all connects.

42
00:02:46.653 --> 00:02:51.599
First the requirements and the vendor, then the test, the go-live and the use.

43
00:02:52.629 --> 00:02:54.371
Everything points at go-live.

44
00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:58.104
Choose that day carefully, not in your busiest time.

45
00:02:58.783 --> 00:03:00.467
A mistake costs most then.

46
00:03:01.759 --> 00:03:03.384
This is the map of Projects.

47
00:03:04.102 --> 00:03:08.119
Leading IT projects is the fourth station of IT and agile.

48
00:03:09.168 --> 00:03:13.092
Leading IT projects has four topics, each with four levels.

49
00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:16.096
Start with Requirements and scope.

50
00:03:16.839 --> 00:03:19.428
At Basics level it is about a requirement,

51
00:03:19.591 --> 00:03:22.714
SaaS, the roll-out and the user acceptance test.

52
00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.159
At Working knowledge you add the MVP,

53
00:03:26.298 --> 00:03:29.955
vendor selection, data migration and exit criteria.

54
00:03:31.002 --> 00:03:34.264
At Advanced you add standard or custom, the total cost,

55
00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.273
the cutover weekend and training.

56
00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:40.499
At Expert you add a fixed date with flexible scope,

57
00:03:40.685 --> 00:03:43.634
the contract, hypercare and measuring adoption.

58
00:03:44.688 --> 00:03:48.752
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
